    "turn_text": "America is worth it. Now is the time. America needs your involvement. Please take our pledge to pray, vote, and engage. Join with a movement of other Christians that are doing these three simple things that can really impact this nation. Join us. We are here starting a new series on prayer and intercession. I really feel like we are all carrying burdens for our nation right now. And before we get later in the fall, I want to focus in with some incredible people about the burden of prayer for our nation. How do we actually carry a nation in prayer? So many times we think about You know, praying for myself, all my needs. We pray for our families. We pray for our churches. But when you really start thinking about praying for your city, your county, your state and your nation, does that even make sense? But you know what? God wants us to pray big prayers. And a lot of us, you know, we watch the news and we start Thinking about, wow, that's an injustice we're experiencing. That's something's not right. And we see it, we have discernment, we have wisdom because we have the Holy Spirit inside of us as born-again Christians. We see things, but what do we actually do with it? A lot of times we turn it into anger, we turn it into fear because we're not taking these things to the Lord. So today, we're going to start this series with Congresswoman Vicki Hartzler. Now, Congresswoman Vicki, she served in Missouri 04. She was elected to Congress in 2010 and served until 2023. What I love about Vicki is she's a real believer. She's a real Christian and she also served on the armed services committee and also worked as the head of the values action caucus really working on family values in congress the whole time she served there. Vicki, I am so thrilled to have you today. Oh, I'm honored to be here. This is great. Well, I want to start with the beginning of your story. Share with us a little bit about your spiritual life, how you came to know the Lord and also how you decided to run for office for state rep",
