    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's been a blessing. I grew up in a Christian home knowing about God praying to him, but when I was nine years old, I made him my own Lord and asked him to be in charge of my life and to forgive me and prayed with my dad. And it was very, very special and God's been my source of strength and encouragement and counsel. And Jesus has been my best friend ever since. And I'm so grateful, so grateful for that and the highs and lows of my life. He's been there and has through his Holy Spirit been a comforter and encourager and guidance. But soon after I asked Jesus in my heart when I was nine, I was playing outside on our farm, making mud pies and talking to God going, what do you want me to be when I grew up? Because I knew I wanted to be a wife and a mother, but Was there something else that I could do to make a difference for him and for others? And I thought of a couple of things and then the thought came very strong in my head that I could be, you could be a state representative and I thought, yeah, maybe that's something I can",
