    "turn_text": "right. So then the words of Isaiah came to mind, who will go for us? Who will I send? And I said, send me if you can use me. So that began the journey of learning to campaign and campaigning and praying as you go down the street. And God ended up blessing those efforts. And it was his will that I served to. And I believe he gave a ministry of public service. Yeah. And Romans talks about those in authority and he says, they are God's servant, but one version of the Bible says, here's God's, they are God's minister to do you good. Yeah. And they don't bear the sword for nothing, but they're also an agent of wrath to punish their God's minister to punish the wrongdoer. And I believe overall that's the role of elected officials is to do people good and to keep them safe, law and order. But it was a ministry and I enjoyed that, served six years, blessed, became a mom and decided to be a full-time stay-at-home mom and to not run for re-election. So I did that for nine years and volunteered in many ways and then God asked me to and people asked me to run for Congress. I hadn't pictured that. But in 2010, I was asked and after prayer decide, I was supposed to, and I ended up running against a 34-year incumbent chairman of the Armed Services Committee, one of the most powerful people in Washington, D.C., but he wasn't representing our values anymore and was part of the problem. So we ran and the Lord blessed it, and we won, and I was so blessed and honored to serve six terms",
